      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here is a [brief](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/refs/heads/main/chip/npcx/config_chip-npcx9.h#10) for our chip naming rule.\nUsually, we skip package code (replace it with \u0027M\u0027 character) to reduce the complexity. The RAM size code is crucial since it influences the memory map layout and valid ram size. Hence, I suggest renaming it as `NPCX9M3S`. (You also can find out it has the same ram usage with `NPCX9M3X`. But the last character represents its specific features.)",
      "revId": "74dce181fd3d1f85a932116049135563ff1e9a06",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "277b5097_655e0816",
        "filename": "util/ecst.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T02:23:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The following is my suggestion if the base address is 0x10080000.\n```\n#define NPCX9M3S_RAM_ADDR 0x10080000\n#define NPCX9M3S_RAM_SIZE 0x50000\n```\nBut if your target is NPCX9M8S (from the previous discussion), here is my suggestion.\n```\n#define NPCX9M8S_RAM_ADDR 0x10050000\n#define NPCX9M8S_RAM_SIZE 0x80000\n```\n\nPlease notice the layout for code/data ram is 448k/64k bytes. (On chromebook, we used to reserve 64 data ram bytes. The size of code/data ram is adjustable on npcx ec if its total ram size meets the spec, 512k bytes.) And we also need to update the change if the target is NPCX9M8S in chip/npcx/config_chip-npcx9.h.\n```\n/*\n * 448KB program RAM, 1MB of Flash.\n */\n#define NPCX_PROGRAM_MEMORY_SIZE (448 * 1024 - 0x1000)\n/* program memory base address for Code RAM (0x100C0000 - 448KB) */\n#define CONFIG_PROGRAM_MEMORY_BASE 0x10050000\n#define CONFIG_RAM_BASE 0x200C0000 /* memory address of data ram */\n/* Two blocks of data RAM - total size is 64KB */\n#define CONFIG_DATA_RAM_SIZE 0x00010000\n#define CONFIG_RAM_SIZE CONFIG_DATA_RAM_SIZE\n\n/* Override default NPCX_RAM_SIZE because we\u0027re excluding a block. */\n#undef NPCX_RAM_SIZE\n#define NPCX_RAM_SIZE (CONFIG_DATA_RAM_SIZE + NPCX_PROGRAM_MEMORY_SIZE + 0x1000)\n```\n```",
      "revId": "74dce181fd3d1f85a932116049135563ff1e9a06",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
